  TWO DISTINCT GAPS — keep them separate:
    packing  2.110 -> 1.600 = 0.510 bits/param  <- LARGE. your methods line.
    entropy  1.600 -> 1.580 = 0.020 bits/param  <- negligible. the dead end.
  base-3 packing achieves 1.600 (=8/5), NOT the 1.585 log2(3) floor.
  Caveat: 2.110 includes FTerViT's scale overhead; packing touches only the
  code bits, so the realistic win is ~19-24%. Decompose before quoting it.

